<title>COLOMBIA: Banco Industrial Colombiano net profits down.</title>
<headline>Banco Industrial Colombiano net profits down.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's Banco Industrial Colombiano, the sixth largest in terms of assets, reported the following results for 1996 in a statement Wednesday.</p>
<p>Net profits 44.3 billion pesos in 1996 vs 61.29 billion</p>
<p>Proposed dividend of 21 pesos per month per share through 1997. NOTE: Figures are subject to approval by Colombia's securities superintendency.</p>
<p>((--Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom 571 610 7944))</p>
</text>
